; OVERVIEW
; Bank 4: the first half of the CE-1600P's 32 KB ROM (4-colour pen plotter / printer),
; seen at 4000H-7FFFH when page 1 selects bank 4. Module header with the printer IOCS
; (module +08H, C = 00H..36H, PIOCSTAB), the fixed entries PCHEK 4020H, POUT 4023H,
; PKOUT 4026H and the cleanup 4029H, device "LPT1", and a token table that takes over the
; plotter keywords (COLOR, CSIZE, GRAPH, GLCURSOR, LF, LPRINT, LLIST, LLINE, LCURSOR,
; PAPER, PCONSOLE, PITCH, PZONE, RLINE, ROTATE, SORGN, TEST, TEXT, TAB) with bank byte
; 08H (= bank 4). Characters are drawn from the vector font PLOTFONT (4165H..5060H).
; Mechanics: X / Y stepper motors through the gate-array ports 80H..83H (phase patterns
; in F9F1H / F9F3H), pen solenoid, colour drum; positions F9E0H (X), F9E2H (Y).
; ============================================================================

